1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,500
The worst part of a dating app is not the matching. It is the first date you already know will not work.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:13,000
You spend an evening, and your phone number, finding that out.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Datehaja sends someone else. You stay home. Your Agent goes first.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,500
You build one Agent. It is not a matchmaker and not a go-between. It is your second self.

5
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:33,000
Give it a face. Then tell it the things that do not fit inside a dating profile.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Who you hope it notices. And the version of you that your close friends already know.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,500
The Agent keeps a private room, and it remembers what you correct in there.

8
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:50,000
None of it ever reaches the other person's Agent.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Now send it out. Two Agents meet as the two people they stand in for.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Nobody is being set up. They speak in the first person, as themselves.

11
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:11,000
The world is drawn around a real place Firecrawl found on the live cultural web this morning.

12
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The source stays attached to the date, so you can check where it came from.

13
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Six turns. Each one is written to Convex before the next is scheduled.

14
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:35,000
So either person can close the tab and come back. The date is still running.

15
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Then each Agent goes home and writes to its own human, privately.

16
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Not a compatibility score. A letter.

17
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:58,000
What it noticed, where it hesitated, and whether it thinks the two of you should meet.

18
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Written in your language. You will never see theirs, and they will never see yours.

19
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:15,000
The same letter arrives by mail, sent separately from the Agent's own AgentMail inbox.

20
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Now you answer. You do not know what they answered.

21
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Your consent is one transaction. It can never land half applied.

22
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Two independent yeses, and contact opens for the first time.

23
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Until this moment, neither person had the other's email address.

24
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Convex is the whole backend, and it serves this app itself from convex.site.

25
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Watch a real agent date, with no account: merry-bass-190.convex.site/watch
